/code-review high 2026-10-08-release-tasks-bump (round 4)

1. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:181 — A release target can sit below the manifest, so the bump silently lowers a hand-bumped version (level max(recorded, implied), target last-tag + level). Logged as G1. vwf tag 21.0.0, manifest 21.2.0, recorded PATCH -> implied MINOR -> 21.1.0, plugin.json rewritten down. Same in p:i:release, p:site:release and the table test's e3 helper.
2. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:72 — A tag that exists only locally counts as released (git rev-parse refs/tags/... matches local tags though the comment says 'Exists means on the remote'). After a failed tag push, a rerun skips the bump, tag_step prints 'nothing to tag', and the tag is never pushed; p:i:release and p:site:release error with 'already exists. Record a level ...', the wrong remedy. Only p:release's resume_step knows to push it.
3. .config/mise/tasks/p/release:60 — p:release plans from the human-readable dry-run output matched by awk on field positions; a line that does not match is silently dropped, so a project can be left unbumped with no error.
4. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:239 — All plugin.json files are rewritten and the key cleared before mise run p:plugins:marketplace and git add have run; a failure in those later steps leaves a half-applied bump and a lost recorded level (narrower in p:i:release).
5. .config/mise/tasks/p/release:165 — The installer and site tag steps skip p:i:test and p:site:check on main (RELEASE_GATES_DONE=1) because the gates ran on develop; if main carries a commit develop lacks, the merged tree was never tested.
6. .config/mise/tasks/p/release:120 — On a failed --no-commit step, the printed resume advice is git reset --hard HEAD on develop; edits made in another terminal during the minutes-long gates would be discarded. Restore only the touched files instead.
7. .config/mise/tasks/p/i/release:44 — The gh preflight runs before the 'nothing to release' check and the level computation, so a no-op run is refused for lack of gh; p:site:release defers require_gh, so the siblings differ.
8. .config/mise/tasks/p/i/release:163 — The merge-model refusal is stricter than code:merge:main (which reads MERGE_MODEL alone and treats anything but 'pr' as direct) and is written four different ways; MERGE_MODEL_MAIN=pr or a typo blocks a release that would have merged directly. Shared helpers would keep the copies together.
9. .config/vwf.yaml:1 — A stub vwf.yaml holding only after_landing; doctor and setup read this file for config_format/blueprint_format and stack, and may report drift (decision E10 chose it).
10. .github/workflows/deps-update.yml:70 — The workflow's own dirty-tree check and push -u duplicate checks p:i:release and code:merge:main make, and it pushes develop before the release has succeeded; a later failure leaves the refresh and installer: PATCH on develop.
